<http://data.silknow.org/object/81a98633-de7f-3baa-860e-4f603246f8e9>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Textile panel of silk damask, France, 1750-1800."@en , "Textile panel of crimson silk damask. Woven with a large floral pattern of stems with large blooms twisting across a lacy ribbon. There is one print repeat in the width of the textile. In the compartment, formed by the meandering stems and the ribbons, there is a plant with three flowers and three leaves. There are selvedges on each side. The selvedge consist of 2.5 mm of satin with a twill effect, from the binding of groups of threads at intervals, and 5.5 mm woven in tabby, 18 threads of crimson tabby, then 12 outer threads with a white silk warp. There is no outer cordonnet."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c1b53a83-eac3-318e-8d80-c1b2d882842e> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Textile panel of crimson silk damask. Woven with a large floral pattern of stems with large blooms twisting across a lacy ribbon. There is one print repeat in the width of the textile. In the compartment, formed by the meandering stems and the ribbons, there is a plant with three flowers and three leaves. There are selvedges on each side. The selvedge consist of 2.5 mm of satin with a twill effect, from the binding of groups of threads at intervals, and 5.5 mm woven in tabby, 18 threads of crimson tabby, then 12 outer threads with a white silk warp. There is no outer cordonnet."@en , "Textile panel of silk damask, France, 1750-1800."@en ;
